---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout current="harness-engineering" title="Harness engineering">
  <section class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Runtime discipline</p>
      <h1>Harness engineering: where agents become software.</h1>
      <p>
        The harness is the boundary around the model. It decides what context
        enters, what actions are allowed, how state changes, and what evidence
        is kept after every turn.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="harness-map" aria-label="Agent harness responsibility map">
      <div class="harness-lane">
        <span>Inputs</span>
        <strong>User goal</strong>
        <strong>Session state</strong>
        <strong>Available tools</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="harness-core">
        <span>Harness</span>
        <h3>Controlled execution boundary</h3>
        <div>
          <strong>Build context</strong>
          <strong>Route tools</strong>
          <strong>Gate actions</strong>
          <strong>Commit events</strong>
          <strong>Stop or continue</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="harness-lane">
        <span>Outputs</span>
        <strong>Observations</strong>
        <strong>Artifacts</strong>
        <strong>Trace + eval data</strong>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="detail-grid">
      <article class="detail-card">
        <span>Not just prompting</span>
        <h3>The model should not own the system boundary.</h3>
        <p>
          Prompts describe behavior. The harness enforces behavior: tool
          availability, permissions, timeouts, retries, state writes, and
          approval gates.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="detail-card">
        <span>Lifecycle</span>
        <h3>Every turn has a beginning and an end.</h3>
        <p>
          A harness creates or loads a session, appends the user event, invokes
          the agent, records intermediate events, commits state changes, and
          returns the final response.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="detail-card">
        <span>Replay</span>
        <h3>If it cannot be replayed, it cannot be trusted.</h3>
        <p>
          Store enough evidence to reconstruct the run: model config, prompt
          inputs, tool calls, tool outputs, errors, approvals, and final answer.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="signal-panel">
      <h3>Harness responsibilities</h3>
      <div>
        <article>
          <span>Before model</span>
          <strong>load session, select context, expose tools, apply policy</strong>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>During tools</span>
          <strong>validate arguments, enforce permissions, capture observations</strong>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>After turn</span>
          <strong>commit state, write traces, emit artifacts, prepare eval data</strong>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <a class="next-card" href="/harness-examples/">
      <span>Next</span>
      <strong>Illustrate the harness with Google ADK examples</strong>
    </a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
